  "conformsTo": "http://mlcommons.org/croissant/1.1",
  "name": "Wan2.2-Syn-121x704x1280_32k",
  "description": "\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tFastVideo Synthetic Wan2.2 720P dataset\n\t\n\n\n  \n\n\n  \n    FastVideo Team\u2003\n  \n\n  \n    Paper | \n    Github |\n    Project Page\n  \n\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tAbstract\n\t\n\nScaling video diffusion transformers (DiTs) is limited by their quadratic 3D attention, even though most of the attention mass concentrates on a small subset of positions. We turn this observation into VSA, a trainable, hardware-efficient sparse attention that replaces full attention at \\emph{both} training and inference. In VSA, a\u2026 See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Hahshshsshbs/Wan2.2-Syn-121x704x1280_32k.",
  "alternateName": [
